  "instructions": [
    "Heat olive oil in a large Dutch oven over medium heat.",
    "Add pork cubes and sear until browned on all sides, about 5\u20117 minutes. Transfer to a plate and set aside.",
    "Saut\u00e9 onion, carrots, celery, and garlic in the same pot until vegetables soften, 6\u20118 minutes.",
    "Return pork to the pot. Stir in sauerkraut, beef broth, apple cider vinegar, thyme, paprika, salt, and pepper.",
    "Bring to a gentle simmer, then reduce heat to low, cover, and braise for 1\u00bd\u20112 hours, stirring occasionally, until pork is tender and flavors meld.",
    "Taste and adjust seasoning if needed. Serve hot with crusty bread or boiled potatoes."
